    "Q10.6": "Hearing students describe how being flagged felt like 'surveillance' or a confirmation of their fears, especially regarding accommodations and cultural adaptation, made me realize that the model's technical accuracy is secondary to its social impact. The idea of shifting from prediction to self-awareness dashboards fundamentally changed my view on what an acceptable system looks like; we must prioritize student agency over administrative efficiency."
